From 1f872088600860b561cf549bafded7237aa01a81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericman2001 <ericman2001@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:39:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] remoteproc: qcom: pas: Fall back to the default domain
 without a resource table

Without a hypervisor, the PAS driver asks TrustZone for the resource
table of a remote processor with an IOMMU stream. Chrome OS TrustZone
firmware (HP Googlebook, X1E80100) fails that call with -EIO, so the
ADSP never boots. Mapping only its carveouts isn't enough either: the
ADSP then faults on the peripherals it uses.

Fall back to the default domain of the stream instead, which
arm-smmu-qcom makes an identity mapping. With that, the ADSP boots and
its battery charger service works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index cb3e51d6f..a52c476b6 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -486,8 +486,21 @@ static int qcom_pas_parse_firmware(struct rproc *rproc, const struct firmware *f
 	output_rt = qcom_scm_pas_get_rsc_table(pas->pas_ctx, table, table_sz, &output_rt_size);
 	ret = IS_ERR(output_rt) ? PTR_ERR(output_rt) : 0;
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(pas->dev, "Error in getting resource table: %d\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		/*
+		 * Not all TrustZone firmware can provide the resource table
+		 * (Chrome OS firmware can't). Without it, the remote processor
+		 * can't be confined to its own IOMMU domain, so leave it in
+		 * the default domain of its stream: an identity mapping, as
+		 * given by arm-smmu-qcom.
+		 */
+		dev_info(pas->dev,
+			 "no resource table from TrustZone (%d), using the default IOMMU domain\n",
+			 ret);
+		iommu_detach_device(rproc->domain, rproc->dev.parent);
+		iommu_domain_free(rproc->domain);
+		rproc->domain = NULL;
+		rproc->has_iommu = false;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	kfree(rproc->cached_table);
-- 
